From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nadelacruz-00 <323917690+nadelacruz-00@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:19:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "drm/msm/a6xx: erhai-7.3 b11: do not run the RSCC stop
 on A830 (external abort)"

This reverts commit e9faa3ec4224.

The external abort the original avoided came from the device tree, not the
RSCC stop: the RSCC sits at gpu+0x50000, outside the GPU node's 0x40000
kgsl_3d0_reg_memory window, and the GX GDSC was left unbound by 9c9eefdef1
because the gxclkctl node mapped only 4 KiB; with both windows fixed
a6xx_rpmh_stop() runs the upstream sequence on a8xx again.

Tested on a OnePlus Pad 3 (SM8750) with the whole series: the GPU
powers up at probe (no -19), the CX GDSC collapses on runtime suspend,
IGT msm_recovery gpu-fault recovers in 5 of 5 runs, and 2.5 h of desktop
use ran 3,227 runtime-PM cycles without a GMU wedge.

Signed-off-by: nadelacruz-00 <323917690+nadelacruz-00@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c | 16 ----------------
 1 file changed, 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
index 8699937d154..01367c13e78 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -791,22 +791,6 @@ static void a6xx_rpmh_stop(struct a6xx_gmu *gmu)
 	if (!test_and_clear_bit(GMU_STATUS_FW_START, &gmu->status))
 		return;
 
-	/*
-	 * erhai (Adreno 830 / a8xx): the GPU RSS/RSCC register region is
-	 * unclocked in this low-power state on this board ("dead GX genpd" —
-	 * no gx gdsc, gxclkctl unclaimed), so touching GMU_RSCC_CONTROL_REQ /
-	 * GPU_RSCC_RSC_STATUS0_DRV0 raises an unrecoverable synchronous external
-	 * abort (0x96000007). That Oopses pm_runtime_work (observed on every b10
-	 * boot, incl. healthy ones). The pre-release 7.2 path (before this hunk's
-	 * inversion) never reached the RSCC code for a booted GMU — it cleared
-	 * FW_START and returned. Keep that behavior on a8xx: the GPU is pinned
-	 * always-on on erhai (erhai-gpu-pin), so a runtime suspend should not
-	 * happen at all; if the boot-time race does trigger one, skip the RSCC
-	 * stop instead of faulting.
-	 */
-	if (adreno_is_a8xx(adreno_gpu))
-		return;
-
 	if (adreno_is_a840(adreno_gpu))
 		bitmask = BIT(30);
 
